azonaws.com%2Fee%2Ff8%2Fd29b18994514a479c665dae8d518%2Fimage-10.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1200x675+0+50/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fee%2Ff8%2Fd29b18994514a479c665dae8d518%2Fimage-10.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1200x675+0+50/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fee%2Ff8%2Fd29b18994514a479c665dae8d518%2Fimage-10.jpg" class="img" alt="Elle Fanning as Margo in Margo&amp;#039;s Got Money Troubles." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Elle Fanning in &lt;em&gt;Margo's Got Money Troubles.&lt;/em&gt;                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          &lt;i&gt;Apple TV&lt;/i&gt;                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Apple TV's &lt;em&gt;Margo's Got Money Troubles&lt;/em&gt; is a comedy nominee that doesn't seem like one. But the story of a young woman leaning into problematic choices to build a life with her baby and quirky family was the year's most surprising, energizing show. &lt;em&gt;— Eric Deggans &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommenda