tspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/2000/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe2%2F36%2F00b895f44bd4a47e408f7a0f548b%2F008digitisation.jpg 2000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/2600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe2%2F36%2F00b895f44bd4a47e408f7a0f548b%2F008digitisation.jpg 2600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe2%2F36%2F00b895f44bd4a47e408f7a0f548b%2F008digitisation.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1300px) 1238px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 60px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe2%2F36%2F00b895f44bd4a47e408f7a0f548b%2F008digitisation.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe2%2F36%2F00b895f44bd4a47e408f7a0f548b%2F008digitisation.jpg" class="img" alt="Yazeed Abu Khdeir (left) and Mahmoud Muna work to digitize papers, as Raja Shehadeh (standing) looks on August 2025." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Yazeed Abu Khdeir (left) and Mahmoud Muna work to digitize papers, as Raja Shehadeh (standing) looks on.&lt;br&gt;                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Hannah Harper&lt;br&gt;                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;So he took part in a two-year, discreet effort to spirit them to Scotland, where he has spent many summers. The archives are now at the University of Edinburgh, and the University of Exeter in England has &lt;a href="https://humanities-collections.exeter.ac.uk/dame/s/en/item-set/18465" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;published thousands of pages online&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Shehadeh spoke with NPR's Daniel Estrin about his decades of diary writing, and the secret effort to preserve his archives.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The interview text below has been edited for length and clarity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How keeping a diary consistently for so long impacted who he is as a writer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt; It's been a daily effort...in order to understand better what is happening around me, in order to record and document what is happening. I started when I was...fifteen years old, just before the occupation.  It has been a very good discipline because it helped me understand myself and what's happening around me...I was feeling that we are entering into a historic period that needs to be documented. So I went about writing everything down that was happening and preserving whatever I could preserve.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://humanities-collections.exeter.ac.uk/dame/s/en/item/21011#lg=1&amp;slide=0" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Excerpts from Shehadeh's diary&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; during Israel's invasion of Ramallah at the height of the Palestinian Intifada in 2002&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;April 2, 2002 &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Last night was very noisy. I was awakened many times from the sound of the bombing and shooting ... &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;My mood was not good today. I just got too many telephones. The problem then became that the news spread that my spirits (so it was interpreted are down) so I got more calls from those who thought it is their duty to call me to help raise my morale ...&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I am beginning to feel like a prisoner in the house, in solitary confinement ... I am thinking of exercising by pacing around the house ...&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Then Samer called to say: now they have lifted the curfew ... I was glad to lift the garage door and to turn my car on ... There was absolutely no one on the street. There was dirt and stones and wind and fog but no cars ...&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I continued driving up to the center and then saw two big tanks- how big they look, like elephants in a zoo where they don't belong, parked by our office blocking the street entirely ...&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The satellite stations show the suffering of the Palestinians like a soap opera ... [Palestinian leader Yaser] Arafat is a rebel rouser. He is now very popular and he dramatizes everything. The Palestinians rather than be a force of change are a source of drama and emotionalism throughout the arab world ...&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On Shehadeh's anger at Palestinian leaders for signing a peace accord in the 1990s that didn't stop Israeli settlement expansion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-143027" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2203;         --source-height: 3000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/1000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 1000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/1300/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 1300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/2000/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 2000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/2600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 2600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1300px) 1238px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 60px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/1000/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 1000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/1300/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 1300w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/2000/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 2000w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/2600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg 2600w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1300px) 1238px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 60px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2203x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F59%2Fe898741a4daaa0b73f3e4369c979%2F003archivesample1991.jpg" class="img" alt="Raja Shehadeh’s diary entry for December 2, 1991, written by hand in the Grand Hotel in Washington DC while acting as legal counsel to the Palestinian negotiating team, on notepaper from the Regency Palace hotel, Amman." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Raja Shehadeh's diary entry for December 2, 1991, written by hand in the Grand Hotel in Washington DC while acting as legal counsel to the Palestinian negotiating team, on notepaper from the Regency Palace hotel, Amman.&lt;br&gt;                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Raja Shehadeh                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;My diaries after that point showed a great anger which I was glad I didn't publish. I mean, it was good that I put all my frustration and anger in the diaries because otherwise I would not have been able to live in Palestine because I was so angry and so frustrated by the leadership and so critical of it.  And so the diary played an important role in helping me vent that frustration without getting myself into trouble.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The leadership...didn't realize that the settlements were the disastrous thing and that they had to be stopped, and no agreement should happen without all settlement activities stopped, and they didn't do that.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On his diary entries documenting Israel's expanding control of the West Bank&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt; I started recording the changes in the geography and in the roads and in the landscape and in the effect of the settlements.  I used to walk a lot in the West Bank hills, and after the walks, I would record what I saw and how I felt and how the land looked.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;I was so confused by what was happening and so wanting to understand it, and so writing it helped me understand it. I had my own way and my own nonconformity. And so describing my world in words helped me grasp it better.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shehadeh's fear for the safety of his archives due to Israeli military operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-143031" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1000;         --source-height: 1185;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;         